  "created": "2026-08-28T18:12:19.96Z",
  "description": "FormulaEngineer is a complete .NET Excel solution for high-performance XLSX creation, streaming reading, formula evaluation, and advanced workbook presentation — styling, tables, comments, images, shapes, charts, sparklines, and auto-fit — without Excel or COM.\n\n\t\t\t✓ Accurate formula evaluation — verified against hundreds of real-world formulas; where Excel's cached values exist in source workbooks, results match bit-for-bit\n\t\t\t✓ 461 Excel-compatible functions and special forms across lookup, financial, statistical, math, text, date/time, logical, information, engineering, dynamic-array, lambda-helper, and database families\n\t\t\t✓ Dynamic arrays, structured table references, cross-sheet INDIRECT, spill semantics, and full error propagation\n\t\t\t✓ Ultra-fast, forward-only streaming reader and writer — no loading the entire file into memory\n\t\t\t✓ Professionally styled spreadsheets — fonts, fills, borders, number formats, alignment, layout, protection, and auto-fit\n\t\t\t✓ Advanced reports — conditional formatting, rich text, named styles, themes, and Excel tables\n\t\t\t✓ Workbook presentation objects — notes, threaded comments, images, shapes, charts, and sparklines\n\t\t\t✓ Culture-aware parsing of dates, times, durations, numbers, and booleans\n\t\t\t✓ Shared string deduplication with overflow protection\n\t\t\t✓ Precise ECMA-376 format detection for date/time/duration values\n\t\t\t✓ Safe XML parsing\n\n\t\t\tCross-platform, pure managed code for .NET 6 and later. Ideal for ASP.NET Core Web APIs, Blazor Server/WASM, Windows Forms, WPF, background services, console applications, and serverless environments such as Azure Functions and AWS Lambda.",
